<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48188" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thestĭus</span></b> , ii,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θέστιος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a king of
				Ætolia</i>, <i>father of Leda and
				Althæa</i>, <i>and of Plexippus and
				Toxeus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8, 487</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				77</span></i>; <i><span class="en">155</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">174</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thestĭă-des</span></b> , ae,
				m., <i>a</i> (male) <i>descendant of Thestius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">duo,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Plexippus and Toxeus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 304</span></i>
			 and 434: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">respice Thestiaden,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Meleager</i>, <i>son of
					Althæa</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					5, 305</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thestĭas</span></b> ,
				ădis, f., <i>the daughter of Thestius</i>, i. e. <i>Althæa</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8, 452</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 473</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id.
				Tr. 1, 7, 18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
